Org profile README repo, plus one composite action (actions/claude-review) that is
SHA-pinned by every consumer. There is no build, no lint and no new-user walk.

There IS a test surface, and it is not optional: actions/claude-review/test/ holds a
response-shape harness, a mutant suite and a single-mode identity check. Run ALL
THREE before pushing any change to action.yml, and require every mutant to be caught:

  python3 actions/claude-review/test/harness.py actions/claude-review/action.yml
  python3 actions/claude-review/test/mutants.py actions/claude-review/action.yml \
          actions/claude-review/test/harness.py
  python3 actions/claude-review/test/single_mode_identity.py \
          actions/claude-review/action.yml

Run them ONE AT A TIME. The action writes fixed /tmp paths, so two suites running at
once corrupt each other's request and response files; the harness serialises with a
lock, but do not rely on it to sort out a parallel invocation.

A green harness proves nothing on its own -- a harness that asserts the wrong things
passes just as green as one that works. The mutant run is the non-vacuity control.

The identity check answers the question the other two cannot: not "is the behaviour
correct" but "did it change at all". It replays every single-mode case against a
FROZEN copy of the action at the SHA consumers are pinned to and compares outputs,
body, stdout, stderr and exit code byte for byte. Six required gates depend on
single-mode behaviour. If it goes red, do not regenerate test/baseline/ -- that is
the one edit that turns the whole suite into decoration.

NOT AUTOMATED. This repo has no workflows, so nothing runs any of the above except a
human reading this file. That is a known gap, filed as
